Z||000019||DaRkLoRD||11-12-2000||04:23 PM||||I used to dislike macs as well, but with the way windows has been behaving over the last few years.. I'm seriously considering getting a mac for my next totally new system.. (won't be a while, I'll probably upgrade my trusty old P2-400 a few more times until I can afford a G4.. heh)<P>Or possibly BeOS... that is supposed to be very fast and stable, with lots of available applications. One thing I can't stand is when people suggest I get linux, and say the GIMP is "the same as photoshop"... IT'S NOT!<BR>it's fine for simple graphics, but it's insufficient for professional graphics.. and yes, I have used it before.. I used RedHat 5.2 for several months, and went back to win98 because there were no apps available for linux that were as good as what I was using in windows.. not many games either. Easy enough to fix that however, buy a sega dreamcast or N64.<P>anyway, back on topic.. I've never used WebTV before. Someone mentioned a $50 refurbished WebTV.. where can I buy one of these? Might be fun to play around with it, and see what I can make it do.. (eg. hack the hardware.. upgrade the connection to ethernet or something) <P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||5
Z||000020||william_thorniii||11-13-2000||12:08 PM||||Friends,<P>I don't think that breaking up the page is the best idea either... of course usually long threads just annoy me.  I am much grumpier than my age would lead one to believe. <P>Perhaps by the thread list in each section each page of the thread could be listed below the topic.  It is handled just this way on <A HREF="http://www.woxy.com" TARGET=_blank>www.woxy.com</A>  (my 2nd favorite site).  This allows one to go to the page of intrest and skip all introductory pages.  <P>This does not directly address Stimpy's problem... but if pages are limited to 25 posts, it might be a good way to make it easier to navigate for the rest of us.  <P>William T. Thorn, III ||||reg||5
